/-!
# Monodromy and cyclic holonomy of the finite fiber cover

This module makes the global circuit associated with
`CyclicFiberHop.StepSystem` explicit.  A cover with positive half-period `h`
has exactly `2 * h` directed edges.  Transport around those edges produces one
invertible linear map, the monodromy.  The holonomy group at a phase is the
cyclic subgroup generated by that map.

The natural-number index on `forwardProduct` is intentional.  A bounded index
describes a single displayed lap, but a `Nat` also records the winding count:
after returning to the same phase, further steps apply further monodromy.  The
`OneLapIndex` view below includes both step zero and the completed-circuit
endpoint, while the unbounded product remains the authoritative transport.

There is an exact limitation: this base has only one directed circuit.  Its
holonomy is therefore cyclic (possibly a finite cyclic group or the trivial
group) inside `GL(Fiber3)`.  This construction does **not** realize arbitrary
noncyclic holonomy groups.  Such a model needs a base graph or path groupoid
with more than one independent loop.

A reduction to a chosen ambient subgroup `G` is recorded separately.  Requiring
every local step to lie in `G` forces every path product and monodromy into
`G`.  Merely placing the monodromy at one base phase in an arbitrary subgroup
would not be basepoint invariant: changing the base phase conjugates it, so
one would additionally need invariance under those transport conjugations.
-/


